10 Hooks
********

The hook ‘spofy-player-state-changed-hook’ runs whenever any aspect of
the player state changes: track, play/pause state, shuffle, repeat,
volume, or device.  The mode-line display and dashboard now-playing
section both use this hook to stay up to date.  Add your own functions
to this hook if you want to react to any state change.

   The hook ‘spofy-player-track-changed-hook’ runs only when the current
track changes.  This is a subset of state changes and is useful for
notifications or logging.  The dashboard recently-played section hooks
into this to refresh automatically when the track changes (*note
Dashboard and global control::).  All spofy list buffers (album,
playlist, library tracks, search results, top tracks, recently played,
and artist top tracks) also hook into this to re-render their entries so
the green playing indicator moves to the new track without a manual
refresh.

   The hook ‘spofy-authenticated-hook’ runs once after a successful
OAuth2 authentication.  Use it to perform setup that depends on having a
valid token, such as pre-fetching the user's playlists.


File: spofy.info,  Node: Mode-line display,  Next: Tab-bar display,  Prev: Hooks,  Up: Top

11 Mode-line display
********************

The command ‘spofy-mode-line-mode’ toggles a global minor mode that adds
a spofy segment to the mode line.  The segment shows the currently
playing track formatted according to ‘spofy-mode-line-format’ (*note
Mode-line options: Mode-line.).

   When enabled, the mode hooks into ‘spofy-player-state-changed-hook’
to rebuild the mode-line string whenever the player state changes, then
calls ‘force-mode-line-update’ to refresh all frames.

   The mode is enabled automatically when ‘spofy-global-mode’ is active
and ‘spofy-enable-mode-line’ is non-nil, provided ‘spofy-enable-tab-bar’
is ‘nil’ (*note Global options: Global key and mode-line activation.).
When both options are non-nil, tab-bar display takes precedence and
mode-line display is not enabled.


File: spofy.info,  Node: Tab-bar display,  Next: Development,  Prev: Mode-line display,  Up: Top

12 Tab-bar display
******************

The command ‘spofy-tab-bar-mode’ toggles a global minor mode that adds a
spofy segment to the tab bar.  The segment shows the currently playing
track formatted according to ‘spofy-tab-bar-format’ (*note Tab-bar
options: Tab-bar.).

   When enabled, the mode inserts a ‘tab-bar-format-spofy’ entry into
‘tab-bar-format’ at a position determined by ‘spofy-tab-bar-alignment’
(*note Tab-bar options: Tab-bar.).  The segment is computed fresh on
each tab-bar render, so it automatically adapts when other tab-bar
elements appear or disappear.  Player state changes and theme changes
trigger a re-render, and when the format string contains ‘%G’ or ‘%T’, a
1-second timer keeps the progress bar updating smoothly.  When disabled,
the mode removes the entry, stops the progress timer, and cleans up any
‘tab-bar-format-align-right’ entry that was added automatically.

   The mode is enabled automatically when ‘spofy-global-mode’ is active
and ‘spofy-enable-tab-bar’ is non-nil (*note Global options: Global key
and mode-line activation.).  When enabled, it takes precedence over the
mode-line display to avoid showing track information twice.


